SUMMARY:JOIN THE WAITLIST -  ESL English X Korean Language Exchange\, Clas
 s & Games
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class\n**\\
 #\\#\\# ⚠️ If the class is listed as full\\\, PLEASE JOIN the waitlist
  and we will let guests in based on the class’ needs to balance the numb
 er of Korean & English speakers\\!**\n\n**\\#\\#\\# 👨‍🏫** **KOREAN
  X ENGLISH LANGUAGE EXCHANGE**\n\n* **Mini English Class with Certified Te
 acher + Board Games 🎲**\n\n**###** **⚠️ Space is VERY LIMITED** **s
 o register ASAP to save your spot!**\n\n***We can only accept a limited nu
 mber of guests due to the venue's space limitations.***\n\n**SPECIAL PROMO
 TION COST:**\nIf this is your first or second class\, the class is **FREE*
 *\, JUST buy 1 item from the Café Princess Menu\n\nIf this is your third 
 class: pay $3 + buy any menu item from the Café Princess menu\n**\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-**\n\n**##
 #** **📍 LOCATION: CAFÉ PRINCESS**\n\n* **5590 Yonge Street\, North Yor
 k**\n* **Across the street from** **FI**NCH SUBWAY STATION\n**near Shopper
 s Drug Mart**\n\n**###** ***📅*** **DATE:** ***Thursday\, September 3\, 
 2026***\n\n* **🕡 Time: 6:30 PM – 8:45 PM**\n\n**Please register ASAP*
 * **if you want to attend on Sept 3rd so we can save your spot!**\n\n*We h
 ad roughly 80 people sign up for the last two events... but we only have s
 pace for 30 people max.*\n**\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-**\n**Aft
 er registering\, please do the following on Sept. 3rd :**\n\n1. **✅ Do y
 our best to arrive on time @ Café Princess (6:30 PM)**\n2. **✅ Tell us 
 whether you want to focus on learning/practicing ENGLISH or KOREAN**\n3. *
 *✅ Tell us your level: Beginner\, Intermediate\, Advanced or Expert**\n4
 . **✅** **Buy 1 item from the Café Princess Menu** (This is the only co
 st if this is your 1st or 2nd class. There is an additional $3 fee if this
  is your third class)\n\n**\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-**\n**✨ Popular menu items
  include:**\n\n* ***🍓 Strawberry Cheesecake Bingsu***\n* ***🍧 Mango 
 or Oreo Bingsu***\n* ***☕ Matcha & Tiramisu Lattes***\n* ***🧇 Princes
 s Waffles with Ice Cream & Much More***\n\n**###** **What to Expect**\n\n*
  ***🇰🇷 Guided Korean & English language practice***\n* ***📚 Inter
 active mini-lesson led by an award-winning certified teacher***\n* ***🗣
 ️ Structured conversation activities with native and fluent speakers***\
 n* ***🎲 Board games and social activities to practice language naturall
 y***\n* ***🤝 Make new friends while improving your communication skills
 ***\n\n**###** **Learn From an Expert Language Teacher**\n\n***John Dias (
 OCT\, PhD researcher\, MA\, BEd\, HBA & EELC) is an award-winning certifie
 d language teacher with 10+ years experience***\n\n**###** **Who Should At
 tend?**\n\n* ***English learners (ESL)***\n* ***Native Korean speakers wan
 ting to practice English***\n* ***Korean learners of all levels***\n* ***I
 nternational students\, newcomers\, professionals\, and anyone interested 
 in language and culture***\n\n**Feel free to e-mail [info@tilelearning.com
 ](mailto:info@tilelearning.com) if you have any questions.**\n**Check out 
 our [website](https://www.tilelearning.com/) and [instagram](https://www.i
 nstagram.com/tilelearning/) accounts for more details.**
